{"tool_name":"deepnog","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"deepnog","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa1051"],"license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"Deep learning tool for protein orthologous group assignment","home_url":"https://github.com/univieCUBE/deepnog","keywords":["Protein Sequences","Ortholog"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":600},"biotools":{"id":"deepnog","home":"https://github.com/univieCUBE/deepnog","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"DeepNOG is a tool for protein orthologous groups assignment. Assign proteins to orthologous groups (eggNOG 5) on CPUs or GPUs with deep networks. DeepNOG is much faster than alignment-based methods, providing accuracy similar to HMMER.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T12:16:15Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:41:24.615255Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:deepnog","credit":[{"email":"thomas.rattei@univie.ac.at","name":"Thomas Rattei","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Pairwise sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0491"},{"term":"Pathway analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3928"},{"term":"Protein feature detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3092"}]}],"name":"DeepNOG","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa1051","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Protein orthologous group databases are powerful tools for evolutionary analysis, functional annotation or metabolic pathway modeling across lineages. Sequences are typically assigned to orthologous groups with alignment-based methods, such as profile hidden Markov models, which have become a computational bottleneck. Results: We present DeepNOG, an extremely fast and accurate, alignment-free orthology assignment method based on deep convolutional networks. We compare DeepNOG against state-of-the-art alignment-based (HMMER, DIAMOND) and alignment-free methods (DeepFam) on two orthology databases (COG, eggNOG 5). DeepNOG can be scaled to large orthology databases like eggNOG, for which it outperforms DeepFam in terms of precision and recall by large margins. While alignment-based methods still provide the most accurate assignments among the investigated methods, computing time of DeepNOG is an order of magnitude lower on CPUs. Optional GPU usage further increases throughput massively. A command-line tool enables rapid adoption by users. Availabilityand implementation: Source code and packages are freely available at https://github.com/univieCUBE/deepnog. Install the platform-independent Python program with $pip install deepnog.","authors":[{"name":"Feldbauer R."},{"name":"Flexer A."},{"name":"Gosch L."},{"name":"Hyden P."},{"name":"Luftinger L."},{"name":"Rattei T."}],"citationCount":18,"date":"2020-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"DeepNOG: Fast and accurate protein orthologous group assignment"},"pmcid":"PMC8016488","pmid":"33367584"}],"topic":[{"term":"Endocrinology and metabolism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3407"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Proteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0078"},{"term":"Sequence sites, features and motifs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0160"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"DeepNOG","home":"https://bio.tools/deepnog","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"DeepNOG is a tool for protein orthologous groups assignment. Assign proteins to orthologous groups (eggNOG 5) on CPUs or GPUs with deep networks. DeepNOG is much faster than alignment-based methods, providing accuracy similar to HMMER.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:deepnog/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"bi